# Public mobile configuration only. This file is a TEMPLATE, not a live environment.
#
# Set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL to the NestJS backend origin, including /api.
# Do not use Next.js /api/proxy/.
# Do not put secrets, JWT keys, GeePay credentials, or RTSA passwords in EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables.
#
# Development / UAT:
#   Set this explicitly in mobile/.env (gitignored) before starting Expo.
#   On a physical Expo Go device, do not use localhost.
#   Example UAT (set in .env only, never treat as a production default):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://uat-api-vensure.ventureholdingltd.com/api
#
# Local LAN backend example:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3001/api
#
# Production / release:
#   preview EAS profile stays on UAT (see eas.json).
#   production-apk and production EAS profiles use:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api-vensure.ventureholdingltd.com/api
#   Production APP_ENV=production rejects UAT, localhost, and 192.168.* URLs.
#   A missing value in a production/release build fails fast.
#
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
